   "title": "Attributes and wrangle (read me)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Attributes are named values stored on points or faces. This graph creates some, edits them with an expression, colours by one and builds a group from it.\n\n1) Attribute Create writes 'dist' = distance from the origin (expression length(@P)).\n2) Attribute Noise writes a second attribute, 'height' (0 to 1), instead of moving P.\n3) Wrangle edits it with Python-like code: heights fade out towards the edge using @dist.\n4) Attribute Promote copies 'height' from points to faces, because the next two nodes work on faces.\n5) Group Create puts every face with @height > 0.35 into the group 'tall'; PolyExtrude raises only those faces, each by its own height (Local Attributes on, Distance Scale = height).\n6) Color 'Ramp from Attribute' maps height to a blue-to-red ramp.\n\nTweak: the group threshold, the noise Element Size and Seed, the extrude Distance, or the Wrangle code."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
